course: dictionary
lesson: 2918
title: What drainage means
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Drainage is the way water or other liquid flows away from a place. Think about rain falling on a playground: where does it go? It can run into pipes, into ditches, or soak into the soil. All of these are drainage.
explain: Drainage can also mean the system of pipes and ditches that carries rainwater or waste water away. When drainage is poor, water cannot leave and stays in puddles or floods the ground.
explain: Read this sentence: «A drainage basin is all the land whose water drains into one river.» Basin is the land, and drainage is the water flowing off it. Check your meaning by swapping it in: "all the land whose water flows away into one river" still makes sense, so you are right.
fact: Drainage means the way water or other liquid flows away from a place.
fact: A «drainage basin» is all the land whose water drains into one river.
fact: «Tributaries» are small streams that join a river on the way, so the river grows bigger as it flows downhill.
fact: Good drainage helps garden plants, because soil that drains well does not stay soggy around the roots.
fact: In medicine, drainage means letting fluid out of a wound or part of the body. Drainage is usually not a word with a plural.
exercise: «A river collects water from all the land that slopes towards it, called its drainage basin.» What is a drainage basin? | A small stream that joins a river | *All the land whose water drains into one river | A type of pipe used under roads | A deep hole in the ground where a river starts
exercise: A gardener says, «The bed needs good drainage.» What does good drainage help the plants with? | *Water flows away, so the roots do not sit in soggy soil | The flowers get brighter colours | The soil dries out completely and never holds any water | The rain stops falling on the plants
exercise: «Small streams called tributaries join it on the way, so it grows bigger as it flows downhill.» Find and copy the word for the small streams that join a river. | downhill | *tributaries | river | streams
test: What is a drainage system? | A map showing the rivers in a country | A type of plant that grows near water | *The pipes and ditches that carry away rainwater or waste water | A tool for digging holes in the garden
test: Why might a town flood when its drainage is poor? | Poor drainage stops rain from falling | *The water has nowhere to go, so it builds up | Floods only happen near the sea | The water flows away too fast into the sky
exam: «Poor drainage meant the field was soggy after every shower.» What does drainage mean here? | *Water flows away quickly down the hill, leaving the field dry | The field is covered in tall grass | The field is very hot and dry all year | Water does not flow away well, so the field stays wet
